        <mxCell id="fI3IS1DAUvFwtO677m2t-3" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h2&gt;The Prepaid model uses Deferred Revenue model for Revenue recognition.&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;Here the customer pays upfront for $300, and the cash is deposited in the Bank / Cash account (Asset) as Debit.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;The Unearned Revenue account (Liability) is credited with the same amount.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 15px;&quot;&gt;On consuming the services by the customer, the revenue is recognized. Now the Revenue account gets debited after a fixed no of reconciliation days, lets say 1 day for $10 per day until usage bucket is exhausted and Unearned Revenue account gets credited by $10 each day reducing the liability.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="600" x="-560" y="2010" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
